# {% if is_codex %}@hm-loop-p5-batch{% else %}/hm:loop-p5-batch{% endif %} — prompt-driven SPEC bulk authoring (PLAN-total-spec-coverage ADR-013 R2)

Extracted from the standard `/hm:loop` body (ADR-006 of
PLAN-latency-worktree-step-preview) to keep the per-iter loop lean — the P5-batch
path is a niche bulk-authoring mode, not part of the normal iteration body. The
standard loop dispatches here when `<goal>` begins with `p5-batch`
(e.g. `/hm:loop p5-batch-1`, `/hm:loop p5-batch-all`). This path is NOT routed
through `autoloop_driver.run()` — ADR-013 R2 explicitly requires the slash
command to handle batching here.

> **Worktree precondition.** When reached via `/hm:loop p5-batch-N`, the loop
> already engaged `<WT>` at its step 5 and commits at loop close (step 7). When
> this command is invoked **directly**, no loop steps ran — engage a worktree
> first (`worktree create execute "$(pwd)"`) or operate in cwd, and commit via
> `/hm:wrapup`.
